{"Title":"An Act relative to the Gaming Commission having at least 1 commissioner be a resident of western Massachusetts","BillNumber":"H424","DocketNumber":"HD618","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BLW1","Name":"Bud L. Williams","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BLW1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-14T04:42:01.31"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BLW1","Name":"Bud L. Williams","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BLW1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-14T04:42:01.31"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H424/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Williams of Springfield, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 424) of Bud L. Williams for legislation to require that at least one member of the Gaming Commission be a current full-time resident of Hampden, Hampshire, Franklin, or Berkshire counties.  Economic Development and Emerging Technologies.","DocumentText":"\tSubsection (a) of section 3 of chapter 23K of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the first sentence the following sentence:- At least 1 of the 5 commissioners shall be, upon appointment, a current full time resident of Hampden, Hampshire, Franklin or Berkshire county.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J12","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J12"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}